      en: "A Dutch fort on the coast in Senya Beraku, established to promote the gold, ivory, and slave trade. Built in 1667. Originally called 'Fort de Goede Hoop'. The last fort built by the Dutch in Ghana. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Ghana — a country shaped by its Atlantic coastline, the Volta river system, the legacy of the Ashanti Kingdom, and its cocoa and gold wealth — and offers insight into the regional identity. Located in the West African state of Ghana along the Gulf of Guinea coast."
